.TH "SI" "1" "" "SI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
si \- parse and convert SI units
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[CR]si\f[R] [\f[CR]OPTION\f[R]]\&...
[\f[CR]EXPRESSION\f[R]]\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]si\f[R] parses expressions containing SI units and converts
between compatible units.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-c\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-completions\f[R] \f[I]SHELL\f[R]
Generate shell completions.
Supported values are \f[CR]bash\f[R] and \f[CR]zsh\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-n\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-notation\f[R] \f[I]NOTATION\f[R]
Set numeric notation.
Supported values are \f[CR]general\f[R], \f[CR]fixed\f[R],
\f[CR]scientific\f[R], \f[CR]e\f[R], and \f[CR]E\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-o\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-output\f[R] \f[I]FORMAT\f[R]
Set output format.
Supported values are \f[CR]utf\f[R], \f[CR]ascii\f[R], and
\f[CR]json\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-p\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-precision\f[R] \f[I]NUMBER\f[R]
Set decimal precision (default: 3).
.TP
\f[CR]\-u\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-unit\f[R] \f[I]STRING\f[R]
Convert the quantity to the specified target unit representation.
.TP
\f[CR]\-s\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-strict\f[R]
Enforce strict TeX\-style parsing rules for values.
.TP
\f[CR]\-b\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-base\f[R]
Format output using SI base units.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-version\f[R]
Display version information.
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Display help information.
.SH EXAMPLES
Parse a quantity:
.IP
.EX
si \(aq9.80665 m/s\(ha2\(aq
>> 9.80665 m/s²
.EE
.PP
Format using ASCII symbols:
.IP
.EX
si \-o=ascii \(aq1.5 kg·cm·s⁻²\(aq
>> 1.5 kg\(rs*cm*s\(ha\-2
.EE
.PP
Use scientific notation with three decimal places:
.IP
.EX
si \-n=scientific \-p=3 \-o=utf \(aq123.456789 kg\(rs*m/s\(ha2\(aq
>> 1.234×10² kg⋅m/s²
.EE
.PP
Format using SI base units:
.IP
.EX
si \-\-base \(aq3.0 ohm\(rs*m\(ha2\(aq
>> 3 kg⋅m⁴⋅s⁻³⋅A⁻²
.EE
.PP
Convert to a target unit:
.IP
.EX
si \-u \(aqWb/mm\(ha2\(aq \(aq10 T\(aq
>> 1×10⁻⁵ Wb/mm²
.EE
.PP
Produce JSON output:
.IP
.EX
si \-o=json \(aq101325 kPa\(aq
>> {\(dqvalue\(dq:101325,\(dqunit\(dq:{\(dqdim\(dq:{\(dqkg\(dq:1,\(dqm\(dq:\-1,\(dqs\(dq:\-2,\(dqA\(dq:0,\(dqK\(dq:0,\(dqmol\(dq:0,\(dqcd\(dq:0},\(dqscale\(dq:1e3}}
.EE
